      "id": "r2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "phons &c. of all the other copies except A. are simple. But in A.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "we have the following more full-bodied and flowery Colophon इति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "श्रीमहाराजाधिराजसामन्तसीमन्तचूडामणिकविशेखरयोगीन्द्रमुकुटमणिराजर्षिश्रीभर्तृहरिविवि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "(sic; clearly a copyist's slip) रचितं वैराग्यशतकं तृतीयं पूर्णतामगमत् ॥[*]",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Let us now proceed to examine Dr. Bhâu's objection. I will",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "let him speak for himself. “He is commonly but erroneous-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "ly supposed to be a brother of Vikrama, as the fifth couplet of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the Vairâgyas'ataka shows viz. : that the author was an eminent",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "poet who was dissatisfied with the reception he met with at the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "courts of several princes whom he visited in hopes of reward.”[†]",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Now this proceeds upon the assumption that whatever sentences",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "occur in a work with the first personal pronoun in them may be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "regarded as containing autobiographical statements. That this may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "be true in some cases and to some extent, I do not for one moment",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "deny. But that, it will be observed, is not enough for the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "summary rejection of the popular belief in this case. Dr. Bhâu",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "treats the Stanza which he quotes as by itself conclusive of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "question. I cannot concur in this procedure. With respect to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "Poems of Horace, a similar attempt has been made to spell out",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "a biography of the author from the materials supplied by what",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "may be called these first-personal-sentences. But that learned",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "translator of Horace, Mr. Theodore Martin, disapproves, and if",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "* Dr. Aufrecht's Catalogue gives a colophon श्रीभर्तृहेममहीस (sic).",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "&c. (p. 134b.) In an old MS. at Kolapore inspected for me by my friend",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Mr. Y. V. Athalye the colophon is as follows : इति श्रीभर्तृहरियोगीन्द्रविरचितायां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "सुभाषितरत्नावल्यां नीतिशतकंसमाप्तम्. This is very like the colophon of N.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Like N. too this MS. has 100 Stanzas under 10 heads of 10 Stanzas each.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "† Journal B. B. R. A. S. January 1862 p. 219. The Stanza is fourth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "in our text. Dr. Bhâu also speaks of Bhartṛihari as one of the “nine",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "gems.” But this is not correct.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
